id: pm-1qkivy
title: "History-derived defect recurrence gate: turn resolved incident patterns into targeted local and hosted CI protections"
description: "The immutable tracker contains repeated defect families—extension alias contract loss, path normalization mismatches, history-cache invalidation regressions, Windows process and lock behavior, CLI liveness, release boundary mismatches, and gates that pass fixtures but fail real systems. Existing tests address individual instances, but no canonical service folds historical issues, resolutions, files, tests, error codes, relationships, and recurrence links into a versioned risk model that selects or requires the relevant checks for a new change. Build this as an SDK policy primitive used identically by local pre-push gates and GitHub Actions. Deterministic rules provide the blocking core; optional semantic clustering may propose families but cannot silently become a blocker."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[9]: "area:ci",cicd,context-management,defect-escape,history,instrument-integrity,quality-gate,recurrence,sdk-first
created_at: "2026-08-03T11:14:27.152Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T20:35:50.121Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "A public SDK recurrence analyzer incrementally folds terminal issues, resolution evidence, linked files and tests, error codes, affected versions, and typed recurrence or supersedes edges into versioned defect families; Every family records canonical owner, trigger signals, required local checks, required hosted checks, negative control, escape budget, false-positive budget, and links to the historical items that justify it; A change-risk command and SDK call accept a commit, file set, package, or pm item and return a bounded explainable receipt naming selected families, evidence paths, required gates, omissions, and token and latency cost; Local pre-push and GitHub Actions consume the same generated policy artifact and fail on drift between their selected checks; hosted CI may add environment-only checks but cannot omit local deterministic checks; The initial backfill covers extension alias contracts, path and slug normalization, history projection invalidation, cross-platform process or lock behavior, CLI liveness, release and registry boundaries, and self-generated fixture blind spots; A closed defect cannot satisfy recurrence governance without a linked regression test, a deterministic non-test gate, or an explicit reviewed waiver with expiry; Optional semantic clustering only proposes families with evidence and confidence; deterministic identifiers, paths, test links, error codes, and typed edges control blocking behavior; The index is cursorable, resumable, merge-safe, and benchmarked on million-item multi-decade histories; incremental change analysis does not scan or serialize the full corpus; Mutation and policy changes append hash-chained history events so any recurrence model version and CI decision can be reconstructed later"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make every resolved defect teach local and hosted CI which failure class must never escape again
value: Historical context becomes an executable quality asset instead of a passive archive
impact: "Reduces recurring regressions while keeping fast local feedback targeted, explainable, and consistent with hosted enforcement"
outcome: "Each changed surface receives a bounded, evidence-linked recurrence risk receipt and the exact deterministic gates required by prior incidents"
why_now: All-status review found repeated families with strong historical evidence but no portfolio owner that converts those relationships into change-aware CI selection
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: medium
